+.. _cli_inserting_data_convert:
+
+Transforming incoming records
+-----------------------------
+
+The ``--convert`` option can be used to run Python code against each incoming
+object before it is inserted. The object is available to the code as ``row``
+and can be modified in place. For example, this increments ``n`` and converts
+it from a string to an integer::
+
+    $ echo '{"name": "Cleo", "n": "2"}' | \
+        sqlite-utils insert data.db rows - \
+        --convert 'row["n"] = int(row["n"]) + 1'
+
+Every input object is inserted, regardless of the value returned by the code.
+
